				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2203795&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045290" alt="Kalinin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2203795)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;" >Kalinin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1471029132 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Aug 2016 19:12</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2557936">
									

<blockquote>
<p>my loving tribute to pulp noir stories, placed in the SCP Foundation setting</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The lampshading made it key that it's not the director lashing out at the detective, but the story lashing out at the genre</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Does not compute.</p>
<p>If this is in fact &quot;the struggle of noir tropes in the Foundationverse,&quot; then it's not doing its job. That's not at all how I read the story, and it doesn't seem like that was at all intended by the author in their initial post. Maybe I'm incorrect, but there's nothing in what's being presented here that leads me to that conclusion.</p>
<p>Even if that is the purpose, there's more elegant ways to do that. It would be like if someone were lampooning 70s/80s cop movies and had a guy going &quot;damn it Callahan, you're just a cop on the edge who plays by his own rules! I'm too old for this shit!&quot; At a certain point you have to rein in the urge to look directly into the camera and wink at the audience.</p>
<p>Further, I don't accept the existence of a &quot;struggle&quot; for noir tropes in the Foundation universe. There's no reason stories like that can't exist here.</p>

							</div>

								
					
