		<div class="post" id="post-2569395">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2569395)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2569395">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1922529&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045290" alt="Agent MacLeod" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1922529)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;" >Agent MacLeod</a></span> <span class="odate time_1471757277 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Aug 2016 05:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2569395">
									

<p>It's entertaining, but, as entertaining as it is, I honestly don't see someone getting away with the kind of shit this guy's pulling in the Foundation. It seems like that's at least part of the point, but still&#8230;</p>
<p>I've worked with hard-drinking and/or hard-smoking men who fancy themselves tough (and in many cases, are). They tend not to act like pulp characters, because, despite often <em>wanting to</em>, just ignoring the rules tends to result in more trouble than they care to deal with (read: they'd rather keep their jobs than their independence). As I said, this seems to acknowledge that it's unrealistic for this sort of guy to last long as an MTF operative/Foundation employee, but the character is still standing, still where he wanted to be, when all's said and done. A story wherein such a character gets knocked down a peg or six might be fun, or a story wherein someone who fancies themselves such a character is forced to face the reality that they're a square just like the rest of us could also be entertaining, but this? Well, I laughed a few times and was&#8230; entertained but my suspension of disbelief was shot, perhaps by the not-quite-4<sup>th</sup>-wall-breaks.</p>
<p>This isn't bad but isn't my thing, is what I'm trying to say.</p>

							</div>

								
					
